# manifest/plugins.list -- one Herdr plugin per line: <owner>/<repo>[/<subdir>] <ref>
#
# The ref is a branch or a tag; Herdr's `--ref` rejects a bare commit and
# records the commit it actually resolved to in plugins.json, which is what
# `diff` compares against to detect a moved ref. See docs/adapters.md and
# the design doc (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-08-herdr-setup-design.md)
# for the full contract. Edit this by hand, or run `herdr-setup absorb`
# after changing plugins on a host to rewrite it from that host's own
# plugins.json.
#
# Written by `herdr-setup absorb` from a host's own Herdr state.
# Edit here, or run `herdr-setup absorb` again to refresh from a host;
# `herdr-setup apply` pushes this content back out to a host.
ezcorp-org/herdr-pc-ram-and-cpu-usage-overlay main
